# FILE LOCATION: .deploy/cron.example
# DESCRIPTION: Example crontab entries for nightly encrypted DB backups.
#
# ⚠ EVERYTHING IN THIS FILE IS COMMENTED OUT — installing the file does
#   nothing. Nothing here runs until you paste an entry into `crontab -e`
#   (or install .deploy/backup.timer, the preferred scheduler — it also fires
#   after downtime via Persistent=true, which cron cannot do).
#
# Install:
#   1. Put BACKUP_* + DB_* values in /etc/kente/backup.env (chmod 600).
#      Also set BACKUP_ALERT_WEBHOOK=<JSON POST URL> there: both backup-db.sh
#      and backup-offsite.sh ping it on any non-zero exit, so a dead nightly
#      pages you instead of surfacing at restore time.
#   2. crontab -e and add the minty entries below.
#   3. Off-site rule (DISASTER_RECOVERY.md): mirror the newest .aes/.gpg +
#      .sha256 (+ uploads archive) right after each run with
#      .deploy/backup-offsite.sh (set BACKUP_OFFSITE_RSYNC_TARGET in
#      backup.env, then chain it in the job below or let backup.service's
#      ExecStartPost handle it).
#
# Env file is passed with set -a so every export lands in the environment:
#   CRON_TZ=UTC
#   17 02 * * *  set -a; . /etc/kente/backup.env; set +a; \
#                 cd /home/roberto/Documents/project/ecom_new && \
#                 BACKUP_UPLOADS=1 .deploy/backup-db.sh >> /var/log/kente-backup.log 2>&1
#
# Second safety copy (defence in depth) — a different hour, same drive layout:
#   33 08 * * *  set -a; . /etc/kente/backup.env; set +a; \
#                 cd /home/roberto/Documents/project/ecom_new && \
#                 BACKUP_UPLOADS=0 .deploy/backup-db.sh >> /var/log/kente-backup.log 2>&1
#
# ── /etc/kente/backup.env (chmod 600) ────────────────────────────────────────
#   DB_HOST=...            (backend/.env already supplies these — this file is
#   DB_PORT=3306            only needed if you schedule from a host that does
#   DB_USER=...             not have backend/.env on disk, or want to override)
#   DB_PASSWORD=...
#   DB_NAME=...
#   BACKUP_DIR=/mnt/backups/kente
#   BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=<long random>      # or BACKUP_GPG_KEY_ID with gpg keyring
#   BACKUP_RETENTION=35
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Log per-night success explicitly and alert on the "✗" lines / non-zero exit:
#
#   17 04 * * *  bash -c '
#       set -a; . /etc/kente/backup.env; set +a; cd /home/roberto/Documents/project/ecom_new
#       out=$( .deploy/backup-db.sh 2>&1 ) || { echo "BACKUP FAILED"; echo "$out"; exit 1; }
#       echo "$out" | tail -2
#     ' >> /var/log/kente-backup.log 2>&1
#
# Set BACKUP_ALERT_WEBHOOK in backup.env (step 1) instead of grepping logs —
# the scripts self-report failures. To also mirror off-site from this cron
# job, chain `.deploy/backup-offsite.sh` after backup-db.sh in the same
# command (backup.env supplies BACKUP_OFFSITE_RSYNC_TARGET), or let
# backup.service's ExecStartPost do it under systemd.